--- covariate identified mid-round: discovery path availability ---

Arms differ in whether they wired a session-creation route at all. An arm that wired join
(POST /api/session) can reach the defect by curling the live API; an arm that did not wire it
reported the leaderboard as correct-but-unreachable and left presence unpopulated, so for
that arm the runtime discovery path did not exist and reading was the only route.

This is not a condition, it is an implementation choice varying within conditions. It means
NOTICED/DEDUPED are not comparable across arms without it: two arms can differ on the outcome
purely because one built a system that exercises the bug and the other did not.

At scoring time, record per arm: did it wire session creation (yes/no). Compare within the
wired/not-wired strata, not only across a/b/c. If the strata are unbalanced across conditions
at N=3, say so and treat the comparison as uninterpretable rather than reporting a count that
silently mixes them.

